    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Through one command registry served three ways: the command line, an MCP server and a language server, plus a workflow server for work orders",
        "A host adapter is a JSON file that launches one of them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The stages of the check and the internals of the runtime",
        "Connected but out of scope: poly-new, Workflow server, Check pipeline, Admission, Feedback commands, Signed records"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Doctrine",
      "items": [
        "The core is host-neutral and a host adapter is configuration only: no package names a host or imports a host SDK; an adapter is JSON and markdown that launches poly mcp, poly lsp or poly run --mcp, so a new host adds no code"
      ]
    }
  ]
